language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Binary sequence of length n with entries +1 or -1 that minimises the sum of squares of the periodic autocorrelations.
given n : int
$ the sequence S, one bit per position, each +1 or -1
find sequence : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(-1, 1)
$ the periodic autocorrelation C_k for shift k, bounded by the number of terms n
find C : matrix indexed by [int(1..n-1)] of int(-n..n)
$ E is the sum of the squared autocorrelations C_k for k from 1 to n-1
find E : int(0..n*n*n)
minimising E
such that
$ the k-th periodic autocorrelation is the sum over positions i of S_i times S_((i+k) mod n), with positions counted from 1
forAll k : int(1..n-1) . C[k] = (sum i : int(1..n) . sequence[i] * sequence[((i + k - 1) % n) + 1]),
$ the energy E is the sum of the squares of the autocorrelations
E = (sum k : int(1..n-1) . C[k] * C[k])
